de9c0-e027-5d60-976f-b886a57bf63c'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Martins inherited George Balanchine’s roles: running the School of American Ballet and City Ballet and choreographing. Should this model persist?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/02/arts/dance/peter-martins-city-ballet-balanchine.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Martins inherited George Balanchine’s roles: running the School of American Ballet and City Ballet and choreographing. Should this model persist?', 'lead_paragraph': 'So Peter Martins, after accusations of sexual harassment and physical and verbal abuse of dancers over decades, has retired from New York City Ballet and the School of American Ballet. An independent investigation of those allegations continues. But this may be the moment to reform the entire job description, and thus to reform ballet.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/arts/03cityballet-notebook/15cityballetnotebook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/03/arts/03cityballet-notebook/15cityballetnotebook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/arts/03cityballet-notebook/15cityballetnotebook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/arts/03cityballet-notebook/15cityballetnotebook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/arts/03cityballet-notebook/15cityballetnotebook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/03/arts/03cityballet-notebook/15cityballetnotebook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/03/arts/03cityballet-notebook/15cityballetnotebook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'History Is About to Change at New York City Ballet. How?', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At City Ballet, History Is About to Change', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martins, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'School of American Ballet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Balanchine, George', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeldon, Christopher', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peck, Justin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-02T15:10:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/858bbc60-14fc-5848-ab38-00997cfa1daa', 'word_count': 1131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/858bbc60-14fc-5848-ab38-00997cfa1daa'}, {'abstract': 'For the comic, who’s being honored by the New York Film Critics Circle, 2017 was a breakthrough year. Her reaction? “Finally it is happening to me.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/02/movies/tiffany-haddish-on-nasty-men-her-snl-feat-and-girls-trip.html', 'snippet': 'For the comic, who’s being honored by the New York Film Critics Circle, 2017 was a breakthrough year. Her reaction? “Finally it is happening to me.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year was a huge one for the actress, comedian and writer Tiffany Haddish, who starred in the hit “Girls Trip” with big-name actresses Queen Latifah, Jada Pinkett Smith and Regina Hall, and stole every scene. Her performance earned her the best supporting actress award from the New York Film Critics Circle, which is handing out the prizes on Wednesday. (She was snubbed by the Golden Globes, to much surprise). She also became the first black female comic to host “Saturday Night Live,” bringing down the house with her infectious energy and sly advice for men accused of sexual misconduct. (“Listen fellas. Listen, O.K.? If you’ve got your thang-thang out, and she got all her clothes on, you’re wrong! You’re in the wrong!”) In December, she spoke with me by phone, while dashing between media appearances in New York.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/04/arts/04bagger-tiffany-haddish/03bagger-tiffany-haddish-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/04/arts/04bagger-tiffany-haddish/03bagger-tiffany-haddish-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i