 '_id': 'nyt://article/7dbfe938-d205-50b1-b1c2-9ce478099de4', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7dbfe938-d205-50b1-b1c2-9ce478099de4'}, {'abstract': 'The journalist on alternative facts, what Putin thinks of Trump and whether the Mueller investigation will be able to prove collusion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/03/magazine/masha-gessen-is-worried-about-outrage-fatigue.html', 'snippet': 'The journalist on alternative facts, what Putin thinks of Trump and whether the Mueller investigation will be able to prove collusion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Your book “The Future Is History” traces the lives of intellectuals following the fall of the Soviet Union and the rise of Vladimir Putin. What do you make of the political climate in the United States, which feels particularly hostile to intellectuals and experts right now? The basic idea of the book — that a people robbed of the tools of self-understanding find themselves at a dead end — actually has relevance to this country. Not that I think Americans are at a dead end, but we should be cognizant of that danger.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/magazine/07mag-talk-promo/07mag-talk-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 334, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/07/magazine/07mag-talk-promo/07mag-talk-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 334}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/magazine/07mag-talk-promo/07mag-talk-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 570, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/magazine/07mag-talk-promo/07mag-talk-promo-superJumbo.jpg