ge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/07/travel/07pecorino1/31pecorino1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/travel/07pecorino1/31pecorino1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/travel/07pecorino1/31pecorino1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/travel/07pecorino1/31pecorino1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/07/travel/07pecorino1/31pecorino1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/travel/07pecorino1/31pecorino1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Going to the Source for a Sacred Italian Cheese', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For This Sacred Italian Cheese, Join the Flock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tuscany (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-03T10:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danielle Pergament', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pergament', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48f1f61d-3388-5406-b87a-d83cfc37d12e', 'word_count': 2223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48f1f61d-3388-5406-b87a-d83cfc37d12e'}, {'abstract': 'Can we teach a computer to predict when it’s time to say goodbye?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/03/magazine/the-dying-algorithm.html', 'snippet': 'Can we teach a computer to predict when it’s time to say goodbye?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of the many small humiliations heaped on a young oncologist in his final year of fellowship, perhaps this one carried the oddest bite: A 2-year-old black-and-white cat named Oscar was apparently better than most doctors at predicting when a terminally ill patient was about to die. The story appeared, astonishingly, in The New England Journal of Medicine in the summer of 2007. Adopted as a kitten by the medical staff, Oscar reigned over one floor of the Steere House nursing home in Rhode Island. When the cat would sniff the air, crane his neck and curl up next to a man or woman, it was a sure sign of impending demise. The doctors would call the families to come in for their last visit. Over the course of several years, the cat had curled up next to 50 patients. Every one of them died shortly thereafter.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/magazine/07mag-onmedicine2-copy/07mag-onmedicine2-articleLarge.png', 'height': 529, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/07/magazine/07mag-onmedicine2-copy/07mag-onmedicine2-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 529}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None