rn village is delighted to be playing its part.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SIDANGKOU, China — By day, the factory workers pound sheets of brass into cylinders and slather metal buttons with glue. By night, they take their creations to the street and begin to play.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/04/world/04China-Saxaphone-sub/merlin_130936514_d9228db9-48d3-48e6-baf6-40756785afde-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/04/world/04China-Saxaphone-sub/merlin_130936514_d9228db9-48d3-48e6-baf6-40756785afde-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/04/world/04China-Saxaphone-sub/merlin_130936514_d9228db9-48d3-48e6-baf6-40756785afde-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/04/world/04China-Saxaphone-sub/merlin_130936514_d9228db9-48d3-48e6-baf6-40756785afde-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/04/world/04China-Saxaphone-sub/merlin_130936514_d9228db9-48d3-48e6-baf6-40756785afde-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/04/world/04China-Saxaphone-sub/merlin_130936514_d9228db9-48d3-48e6-baf6-40756785afde-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/04/world/04China-Saxaphone-sub/merlin_130936514_d9228db9-48d3-48e6-baf6-40756785afde-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s ‘Saxophone Capital,’ a Factory Town Transfixed by Kenny G', 'kicker': 'Sidangkou Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Factory Town in China, Kenny G Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Saxophones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Musical Instruments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sidangkou (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'vis-photo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-03T15:44:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier C. Hernández', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Hernández', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5fc1153-cd14-52f1-9d87-8a7a4fc77a7d', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5fc1153-cd14-52f1-9d87-8a7a4fc77a7d'}, {'abstract': 'Emily Cochrane vets Times reporting. Linda Qiu vets public statements. Both joined The Times at a moment when getting it right has never been more important.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/03/insider/meet-the-washington-bureaus-fact-checkers.html', 'snippet': 'Emily Cochrane vets Times reporting. Linda Qiu vets public statements. Both joined The Times at a moment when getting it right has never been more important.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As far as Emily Cochrane is concerned, there is no Joe Biden. For Ms. Cochrane, per Times style, there is only Joseph R. Biden Jr. Ditto Michael T. Flynn, Eric H. Holder Jr., Roy S. Moore, Robert S. Mueller III, Christopher A. Wray, Michael E. Horowitz, and Donald J. Trump. The comedian Gilbert Gottfried had an old bit where he’d wander into the land of the three-name people, then escape to the land of the one-named people, before finally finding himself in the land of the people with initials in their names. Ms. Cochrane would have felt right at home. “The New York Times has a very specific style in terms of people who use middle initials,” she said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/01/pageoneplus/01a2_itt_factchecking_web/01a2_itt_factchecking_web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/01/pageoneplus/01a2_itt_factchecking_web/01a2_itt_factchecking_web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/01/pageoneplus/01a2_itt_factchecking_web/01a2_itt_factchecking_web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/01/pageoneplus/01a2_itt_factchecking_web/01a2_itt_factchecking_web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 945, 'width': 1413, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/01/pageoneplus/01a2_itt_factchecking_web/01a2_itt_factchecking_web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/01/pageoneplus/01a2_itt_factchecking_web/01a2_itt_factchecking_we