son': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/1ed90c14-2811-55a6-82dc-42904e31511b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/1ed90c14-2811-55a6-82dc-42904e31511b'}, {'abstract': 'Just when you were gearing up to switch to another field, colleagues persuade you to stay on in a fancier role. Big mistake? Now what do you do?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/05/jobs/when-you-take-a-promotion-but-still-want-to-move-on.html', 'snippet': 'Just when you were gearing up to switch to another field, colleagues persuade you to stay on in a fancier role. Big mistake? Now what do you do?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you cannot stand your job, you should be looking for a new one, as actively as possible. Don’t waste time being hard on yourself. It’s often the case that someone who has decided to switch fields entirely must overcome the urge to delay making such a big move.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/business/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo/merlin_131868578_35bac590-79bb-457a-8974-61eac7fd4048-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 504, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/07/business/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo/merlin_131868578_35bac590-79bb-457a-8974-61eac7fd4048-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 504}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/business/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo/merlin_131868578_35bac590-79bb-457a-8974-61eac7fd4048-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 860, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/business/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo/merlin_131868578_35bac590-79bb-457a-8974-61eac7fd4048-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1719, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/business/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/07/business/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/business/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo/07WORKOLOGIST-Illo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When You Take a Promotion, but Still Want to Move On', 'kicker': 'WORKOLOGIST', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When You Accept a Promotion, and Come to Regret It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-05T12:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Walker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c83ce1c-4570-5bee-9fd2-9be42e05f81b', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c83ce1c-4570-5bee-9fd2-9be42e05f81b'}, {'abstract': "With “Blade Runner 2049,” the cinematographer Roger Deakins received his 14th Oscar nomination. He has never won. Here's why he should.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/05/movies/the-bright-and-dark-side-of-roger-deakins.html', 'snippet': "With “Blade Runner 2049,” the cinematographer Roger Deakins received his 14th Oscar nomination. He has never won. Here's why he should.", 'lead_paragraph': 'Would somebody give Roger Deakins an Oscar already? The cinematographer has been wowing us for decades with his vivid, evocative camerawork. His collaborations with the Coen brothers have included the snowy, expansive visuals for “Fargo,” the bleak, modern western feel of “No Country for Old Men” and the  period gritty western feel of “True Grit.” There’s his sweeping imagery for Frank Darabont’s “Shawshank Redemption” and the breathtaking, mystical look he brought to Martin Scorsese’s “Kundun.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/arts/ROGER-DEAKINS1/merlin_128077364_4857ac54-d073-4a4a-842e-c4a5ad8c8718-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/07/arts/ROGER-DEAKINS1/merlin_128077364_4857ac54-d073-4a4a-842e-c4a5ad8c8718-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/arts/ROGER-DEAKINS1/merlin_128077364_4857ac54-d073-4a4a-842e-c4a5ad8c8718-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/arts/ROGER-DEAKINS1/merlin_128077364_4857ac54-d073-4a4a-842e-c4a5ad8c8718-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/arts/ROGER-DEAKINS1/ROGER-DEAKINS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/07/arts/ROGER-DEAKINS1/ROGER-DEAKINS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/07/arts/ROGER-DEAKINS1/ROGER-DEAKINS1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bright (and Dark) Side of Roger Deakins', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bright (and Dark) Side of Roger Deakins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deakins, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Harrison', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gosling, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Villeneuve, Denis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Blade Runner 2049 (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-05T12:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2d6b692-850e-53b5-843f-3a11668ad927', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2d6b692-850e-53b5-843f-3a11668ad927'}, {'abstract': 'For 15 years, Mr. Bloom suffered from chronic fatigue syndrome so severe that he barely got out of bed. But thanks to sleep shifts, pills and exercise, he’s back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/05/nyregion/how-howard-bloom-writer-and-former-publicist-spends-his-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'For 15 years, Mr. Bloom suffered from chronic fatigue syndrome so severe that he barely got out of bed. But thanks to sleep shifts, pills and exercise, he’s back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1980s, Howard Bloom was a fast-talking, headline-making music publicist. But in 1988, he hit a wall. For 15 years, he suffered from chronic fatigue syndrome so severe that he barely got out of bed. “And for five of those years I was too weak to speak and too weak to have another person in the room with me,” Mr. Bloom, now 74, said. Nonetheless, he managed to write three science-related books during those years, and recently published his seventh, “How I Accidentally Started the Sixties,” a memoir of chemical and spiritual experimentation that begins in 1962. Mr. Bloom lives in Park Slope, Brooklyn, where he runs several online discussion groups.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/12/12/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/12/12/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/12/12/nyregion/07ROUTINE1/07ROUTINE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Howard Bloom, Writer and Former Publicist, Spends His Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Odd Hours and Long Walks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloom, Howard (1943- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chronic Fatigue Syndrome', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Slope (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prospect Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-05T12:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7274d6b9-8704-5de0-a1b0-b38aa56eb0e0', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7274d6b9-8704-5de0-a1b0-b38aa56eb0e0'}, {'abstract': 'Last year’s rally has shown few signs of slowing down in 2018. If anything, it appears to be gaining momentum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/05/b