/e6842729-f6c4-5338-b9f8-7262991b1aeb'}, {'abstract': 'There are a host of recent books on battling forgetfulness. Just in time for the new year — and a fresh start — our writer spent a month testing out some of their solutions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/07/books/memory-loss-books.html', 'snippet': 'There are a host of recent books on battling forgetfulness. Just in time for the new year — and a fresh start — our writer spent a month testing out some of their solutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here in the valley of my mid-50s, I try not to get into a swivet over my occasionally faulty memory: Sometimes the mind has a mind of its own. But when I read this chilling passage — “I am dementing. I am dementing. I am dementing.” — from Gerda Saunders’s recent memoir “Memory’s Last Breath: Field Notes on My Dementia,” I found myself starting to panic.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/08/arts/08memorybooks/08Alford-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/08/arts/08memorybooks/08Alford-articleLarge-v2.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/08/arts/08memorybooks/08Alford-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/08/arts/08memorybooks/08Alford-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1260, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/08/arts/08memorybooks/08Alford-thumbStandard-v2.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/08/arts/08memorybooks/08Alford-thumbStandard-v2.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/08/arts/08memorybooks/08memorybooks-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Total Recall: A Reader’s Guide to Memory Gain', 'kicker': 'Reader’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here’s a Test: Remember This Headline Tomorrow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Memory Rescue: Supercharge Your Brain, Reverse Memory Loss and Remember What Matters Most (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Seven Steps to Managing Your Memory: What's Normal, What's Not, and What to Do About It (Book)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AMEN, DANIEL G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Budson, Andrew E', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Connor, Maureen K", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-07T05:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Alford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a0a67fd-5141-5e0a-bd92-17411f5a4b5c', 'word_count': 1175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a0a67fd-5141-5e0a-bd92-17411f5a4b5c'}, {'abstract': 'The couple met in 2014 at a networking event held by the 