Dear Match Book: We Want to Change the World', 'kicker': 'Match Book', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-09T10:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Lamy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lamy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a510b01-2282-5ce5-a98c-3130b57de568', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a510b01-2282-5ce5-a98c-3130b57de568'}, {'abstract': 'A novel exploring a troubled time in the artist’s life is up for discussion at the 92nd Street Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/09/dining/cooking-for-picasso-camille-aubray-92nd-st-y.html', 'snippet': 'A novel exploring a troubled time in the artist’s life is up for discussion at the 92nd Street Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A novel that unpacks a supposedly troubled period in Picasso’s life, “Cooking for Picasso” describes the fictional relationship and mutual inspiration between a young cook and the artist in the South of France in 1936. The author will talk about the food, culture and art she discovered in the region while researching the book: “‘Cooking for Picasso, A Novel’: Camille Aubray in Conversation,” $29, 7 p.m., Jan. 23, 92nd Street Y, 1395 Lexington Avenue (92nd Street), 212-415-5500, 92y.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnerpicasso/merlin_131860142_99447012-0e80-4d0b-a077-64702fae8535-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name'