prosciutto cotto, delicious cooked ham like the highly prized Gran Biscotto line from Rovagnati, made in Lombardy, and now being imported for the first time. Some stores are selling only the delicate plain variety, which is rubbed with herbs and gently steam-cooked; others also sell varieties seasoned with rosemary or studded with black truffle: $18 a pound, Eataly stores; $11.99 for eight ounces (plain), murrayscheese.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnercotto/merlin_131842806_3c00136f-f368-4e50-ae52-7502f3a26068-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 321, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnercotto/merlin_131842806_3c00136f-f368-4e50-ae52-7502f3a26068-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 321}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnercotto/merlin_131842806_3c00136f-f368-4e50-ae52-7502f3a26068-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnercotto/merlin_131842806_3c00136f-f368-4e50-ae52-7502f3a26068-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1095, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnercotto/10burnercotto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnercotto/10burnercotto-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnercotto/10burnercotto-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cotto: A Whole New Meaning for Prosciutto', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Slice: A New Meaning For Prosciutto', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pork', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lombardy (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-09T10:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e931ee0-ff20-59c9-a10a-1ccd6770d49d', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e931ee0-ff20-59c9-a10a-1ccd6770d49d'}, {'abstract': 'Spicy or sweet, ingredients like peanut, melon seed and honey peas await.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/09/dining/west-african-soups-egunsifoods.html', 'snippet': 'Spicy or sweet, ingredients like peanut, melon seed and honey peas await.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A collection of bright West African soups made in Harlem is a good way to put a steaming bowl on the table. Densely textured groundnut (peanut) soup has spicy heat and, thinned a bit, is also excellent cold. Melon seed is the most unusual of the lot, packed with vegetables. Thick Gbegiri, made from Nigerian honey peas, combines mellowness with some chile fire, and does well with chicken added. The smooth, ruddy Obe Ata tomato soup pops with a faintly peppered kick that still shines if you enrich it with some cream: Egunsifoods African soups, Fairway Markets Manhattan (except Kips Bay) and Red Hook, Brooklyn; $8.99 for 17.3 ounces, $40 for four containers (frozen) from egunsifoods.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnersoup/10burnersoup-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnersoup/10burnersoup-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnersoup/10burnersoup-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnersoup/10burnersoup-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1423, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnersoup/10burnersoup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnersoup/10burnersoup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/dining/10burnersoup/10burnersoup-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'West African Soups: When Chicken Noodle Gets Boring', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Heat: West African Soups To Perk Up Bowls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub':