rce-salvadorans-haitians.html', 'snippet': 'The Trump administration’s ending of temporary legal status for Salvadorans and Haitians means that employers who depend on them will have to look harder for help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They clean federal office buildings in Washington and nurse older people in Boston. They are rebuilding hurricane-wrecked Houston. The Atlanta Falcons’ new stadium, plumbing and heating systems at Fannie Mae’s new headquarters, the porterhouse at Peter Luger Steak House and even the Disney World experience have all depended, in small part or large, on their labor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/us/10employers-01/merlin_131982413_7ff5cd67-4f6b-4e24-a83d-408af9d986bd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/10/us/10employers-01/merlin_131982413_7ff5cd67-4f6b-4e24-a83d-408af9d986bd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/us/10employers-01/merlin_131982413_7ff5cd67-4f6b-4e24-a83d-408af9d986bd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/us/10employers-01/merlin_131982413_7ff5cd67-4f6b-4e24-a83d-408af9d986bd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/us/10employers-01/00employers-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/10/us/10employers-01/00employers-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/us/10employers-01/00employers-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Offices to Disney World, Employers Brace for the Loss of an Immigrant Work Force', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loss of Immigrants Will Be Felt Throughout Work Force', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'El Salvador', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salvadoran-Americans', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Haitian-Americans', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Homeland Security Department', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-09T10:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee, Liz Robbins and Caitlin Dickerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dickerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/538dd3e4-328e-5bc9-ac0e-91818b1dbd41', 'word_count': 1537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/538dd3e4-328e-5bc9-ac0e-91818b1dbd41'}, {'abstract': 'People lust after everything from actors to new consumer goods. A vast marketplace caters to some of those desires, and exploits others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/09/magazine/who-decides-whats-sexy-and-who-pays-for-it.html', 'snippet': 'People lust after everything from actors to new consumer goods. A vast marketplace caters to some of those desires, and exploits others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Venus, the goddess of love, has taken many forms, but one dominates. The prehistoric Venus of Willendorf is round, but mostly at the breasts and hips. The Venus de Milo’s missing arms only make her curves more visible. Even the knee length tresses of Botticelli’s Venus fail to conceal her shape. Bounce forward 500 years, and the actress Uma Thurman poses nude, a towering hourglass, in the same oyster shell in “The Adventures of Baron Munchausen.” Some version of this form — white, voluptuous, exposed — is eternally present in our culture, on billboards, on screens, everywhere. This is “sexy,” or at least its usual shorthand. One designed, mainly, by and for straight white men: the fruit of the “male gaze” that the film theorist Laura Mulvey described in 1975, which “projects its fantasy on to the female figure, which is styled accordingly.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/magazine/14mag-firstwords-copy/14mag-14firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'le