'main': 'Bannon, North Korea, El Salvador: Your Tuesday Evening Briefing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Your Evening Briefing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-01-09T23:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Zraick and Sandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zraick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fdfbb53-83ee-5354-a1dc-5b048d598e5b', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fdfbb53-83ee-5354-a1dc-5b048d598e5b'}, {'abstract': 'For nine years, this actor has taken his one-man show on the road like a “time-warp vaudevillian.” What did he learn along the way?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/09/theater/john-lithgow-stories-by-heart-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'For nine years, this actor has taken his one-man show on the road like a “time-warp vaudevillian.” What did he learn along the way?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the spring of 2008, I cooked up a one-man show for myself. In shaping it, I mixed the riotous writing of Ring Lardner and P. G. Wodehouse with stories about my family, my father’s life in the theater and my beginnings as an actor. I performed it for seven consecutive Monday nights at Lincoln Center’s Mitzi Newhouse Theater on the set of somebody else’s play. I called it “Stories By Heart.” It was a pretty slapdash affair, a kind of workshop performance that allowed me to try on a solo show for size.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': '