le': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b6799e6-96c4-5cb8-8699-2342ed6c17f9', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b6799e6-96c4-5cb8-8699-2342ed6c17f9'}, {'abstract': 'The actress on #MeToo, W.E.B. DuBois’ double consciousness and whether or not she’s aged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/10/magazine/gabrielle-union-isnt-done-talking-about-sexual-assault.html', 'snippet': 'The actress on #MeToo, W.E.B. DuBois’ double consciousness and whether or not she’s aged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In your new memoir, “We’re Going to Need More Wine,” you write about your experience being raped at gunpoint while working at a Payless shoe store when you were 19. The book was published as the #MeToo conversation took off, which has placed you at the forefront of the movement to end sexual harassment and assault. I’ve been doing it for two decades, but there were a lot more microphones this time around than there’s ever been. We’re now seeing how many people have dealt with sexual violence and the toll it can take. All of these disclosures — from Hollywood to farmworkers to the restaurant industry to television to music to academia — show that this is so widespread and so many people’s lives have been derailed. All you can think is, I wonder who you could have been and who you can be now? And a lot of those people are waiting for that conversation or for somebody to tell them that they can be anything, that it does not define you.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/magazine/14TALK-promo/14TALK-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/14/magazine/14TALK-promo/14TALK-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/magazine/14TALK-promo/14TALK-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/magazine/14TALK-promo/14TALK-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/magazine/14TALK-promo/14TALK-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/14/magazine/14TALK-promo/14TALK-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/magazine/14TALK-promo/14TALK-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gabrielle Union Isn’t Done Talking About Sexual Assault', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gabrielle Union Isn’t Done Talking About Sexual Assault', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Union, Gabrielle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-10T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Molly Lambert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Molly', 'lastname': 'Lambert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], '