': 'nyt://article/50cfb762-c43a-5a24-a1c4-c33a165df121', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50cfb762-c43a-5a24-a1c4-c33a165df121'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of the film “The Post,” an ode to 1970s office wear. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/10/fashion/9-to-5-dressing-the-post-1970s-office.html', 'snippet': 'In honor of the film “The Post,” an ode to 1970s office wear. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'As movie buffs already know, “The Post,” the Steven Spielberg journalism thriller starring Meryl Streep and Tom Hanks, hits theaters in wide release on Jan. 12. Set in 1971, the film follows the Washington Post’s first female publisher, Katharine Graham, and its editor Ben Bradlee as they grapple with the decision to publish excerpts from the Pentagon Papers. While Mrs. Graham’s unshakable grit and hard-won success would not be easy to emulate, her wardrobe in the film, a veritable tribute to 1970s office wear, is easier to mine. And the pussy-bow blouses and A-line midi-skirts look startlingly fresh in 2018. Here, how to wear these retro staples.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/11/fashion/11browsing-promo/11browsing-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/11/fashion/11browsing-promo/11browsing-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/11/fashion/11browsing-promo/11browsing-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/11/fashion/11browsing-promo/11browsing-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1389, 'width': 20