': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dim the Fluorescents (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Armstrong, Claire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skwarna, Naomi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warth, Daniel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-11T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Castillo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castillo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/02770298-0bac-556d-822a-86a4cf060125', 'word_count': 238, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02770298-0bac-556d-822a-86a4cf060125'}, {'abstract': 'Manfred Kirchheimer’s documentary showcases more than 20 people who give their outlooks on Israel, religion and other topics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/11/movies/my-coffee-with-jewish-friends-review.html', 'snippet': 'Manfred Kirchheimer’s documentary showcases more than 20 people who give their outlooks on Israel, religion and other topics.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Where there are two Jews, there are three opinions,” Manfred Kirchheimer says in his little gem of a documentary, “My Coffee With Jewish Friends.” In the film he speaks with more than 20 people and comes away with countless viewpoints, as well as some smiles and bittersweet tales.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/08/movies/coffee1/merlin_131901065_0f6032be-817f-414b-a5f5-f78e71af0f8a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/08/movies/coffee1/merlin_131901065_