e with his wife, is directed by Howard L. Weiner, a neurology professor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/11/movies/abe-and-phils-last-poker-game-review-martin-landau-paul-sorvino.html', 'snippet': 'The film, about a physician who moves into a nursing home with his wife, is directed by Howard L. Weiner, a neurology professor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reviewing a film after its lead actor’s death is grim even when the movie is good. The best that might be said about “Abe and Phil’s Last Poker Game,” starring Martin Landau, who died in July, is that it might lead viewers to “North by Northwest” or “Ed Wood.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/arts/abe1/abe1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/12/arts/abe1/abe1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/arts/abe1/abe1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/arts/abe1/abe1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 1631, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/arts/abe1/abe1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/12/arts/abe1/abe1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/arts/abe1/abe1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Martin Landau and Paul Sorvino in ‘Abe and Phil’s Last Poker Game’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abe and Phil’s Last Poker Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Abe and Phil's Last Poker Game (Movie)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Howard L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landau, Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorvino, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-11T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6eb1858-420e-5bc1-b2bd-2bd99f90db01', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6eb1858-420e-5bc1-b2bd-2bd99f90db01'}, {'abstract': 'Luka Kain is a find in “Saturday Church,” as a gay teen seeking acceptance and friendship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/11/movies/saturday-church-review.html', 'snippet': 'Luka Kain is a find in “Saturday Church,” as a gay teen seeking acceptance and friendship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ulysses, the young protagonist of “Saturday Church,” is first seen at the burial of his father, a soldier killed overseas. The New York teen, played by Luka Kain, has delicate features and carries an air of quiet about him. He and his younger brother will now be looked after by both their mother Amara (Margot Bingham) and strict Aunt Rose (Regina Taylor). The latter does not mince words after Ulysses is discovered trying on his mother’s shoes. “If I ever hear of you even looking at women’s clothing, I will beat it out of you. You are a man. Start acting like one,” she says, enunciating each word with controlled rage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/movies/12saturdaychurch1/merlin_131901857_0c80d3e8-59d6-4484-8559-1ddbeeef9020-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/12/movies/12saturdaychurch1/merlin_131901857_0c80d3e8-59d6-4484-8559-1ddbeeef9020-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/movies/12saturdaychurch1/merlin_131901857_0c80d3e8-59d6-4484-8559-1ddbeeef9020-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/movies/12saturdaychurch1/merlin_131901857_0c80d3e8-59d6-4484-8559-1ddbeeef9020-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/movies/12saturdaychurch1/saturdaychurch1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/12/movies/12saturdaychurch1/saturdaychurch1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/movies/12saturdaychurch1/saturdaychurch1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Saturday Church,’ Coming of Age, and Coming Out', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saturday Church', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Saturday Church (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cardasis, Damon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Regina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kain, Luka', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-11T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd9edb3d-c637-5335-baca-6f7674b412d5', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd9edb3d-c637-5335-baca-6f7674b412d5'}, {'abstract': 'This documentary from Cullen Hoback will make you think twice about what’s in your tap water.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/11/movies/what-lies-upstream-review.html', 'snippet': 'This documentary from Cullen Hoback will make you think twice about what’s in your tap water.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “What Lies Upstream,” the documentarian Cullen Hoback begins by investigating the 2014 chemical spill that left 300,000 West Virginians without safe tap water. The resulting movie, national in scope, lays out damning (if not always cohesive) arguments about how government regulators tend to defer to the companies they are supposed to supervise, how legislative fixes aren’t permanent and how mandated safety checks are useless if they aren’t performed or performed properly.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/movies/whatlies1/merlin_131903261_7f4489bc-9380-43db-b9ed-f6ec64f2a736-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/10/movies/whatlies1/merlin_131903261_7f4489bc-9380-43db-b9ed-f6ec64f2a736-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/movies/whatlies1/merlin_131903261_7f4489bc-9380-43db-b9ed-f6ec64f2a736-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/movies/whatlies1/merlin_131903261_7f4489bc-9380-43db-b9ed-f6ec64f2a736-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/movies/whatlies1/whatlies1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/10/movies/whatlies1/whatlies1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/10/movies/whatlies1/whatlies1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘What Lies Upstream,’ a Broad View of a Chemical Spill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Lies Upstream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank'