ext at a time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/12/learning/teaching-with-can-texting-save-lives.html', 'snippet': 'Crisis Text Line is upending the suicide hotline, modernizing it for today’s teenagers, one text at a time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this short documentary, “Can Texting Save Lives?”, Times reporters explore the Crisis Text Line, a text-based hotline for crisis intervention that provides counseling 24 hours a day via text messaging to the number 741741.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teaching With: ‘Can Texting Save Lives?’', 'kicker': 'Film Club', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-01-12T10:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caroline Crosson Gilpin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caroline', 'middlename': 'Crosson', 'lastname': 'Gilpin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53ff28b5-70d2-5816-a3b0-2bf4ce076c70', 'word_count': 530, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53ff28b5-70d2-5816-a3b0-2bf4ce076c70'}, {'abstract': 'Late-night hosts had a hard time making light of President Trump’s derogatory characterization of immigrants from Haiti and Africa.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/12/arts/television/trevor-noah-trump-vulgar-comments-immigration.html', 'snippet': 'Late-night hosts had a hard time making light of President Trump’s derogatory characterization of immigrants from Haiti and Africa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to Best of Late Night, a rundown that lets you sleep — and lets us get paid to watch comedy. What do you think of it? What else are you interested in? Let us know: thearts@nytimes.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'c