Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e700462-df14-56ed-bf2a-cb3244df2a15', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e700462-df14-56ed-bf2a-cb3244df2a15'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, people in the room say they heard him make the remarks about “shithole” countries. No, he won’t face any consequences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/12/opinion/trump-shithole-countries-haiti-el-salvador-african-countries-immigration-racism.html', 'snippet': 'Yes, people in the room say they heard him make the remarks about “shithole” countries. No, he won’t face any consequences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I could write a passionate rebuttal extolling all the virtues of Haiti, the island my parents are from, the first free black nation in the Western Hemisphere. I could write about the beauty of the island, the music and vibrant art, the majesty of the mountains, the crystalline blue of the water surrounding her, the resilience of the Haitian people, our incredible work ethic, our faith. I could tell you about my parents, how they came to this country with so many other Haitians, how they embraced the American dream and thrived, how I and so many first-generation Haitian-Americans are products of our parents’ American dreams.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14gayWeb/14gayWeb-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14gayWeb/14gayWeb-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14gayWeb/14gayWeb-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14gayWeb/14gayWeb-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14gayWeb/14gayWeb-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14gayWeb/14gayWeb-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14gayWeb/14gayWeb-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No One Is Coming to Save Us From Trump’s Racism', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No One Is Coming to Save Us From Trump’s Racism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Haitian-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'El Salvador', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-12T17:20:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roxane Gay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roxane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5872e5fd-876a-586b-bf2b-2ea8ed00a95b', 'word_count': 805, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5872e5fd-876a-586b-bf2b-2ea8ed00a95b'}, {'abstract': 'Reports that President Trump called Haiti and African nations “shithole countries” drew nearly universal condemnation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/12/world/africa/africa-trump-shithole.html', 'snippet': 'Reports that President Trump called Haiti and African nations “shithole countries” drew nearly universal condemnation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Governments and citizens across the world recoiled on Friday with disgust, outrage and sadness at reports that President Trump had described Haiti and unspecified African nations as “shithole countries” during a meeting with members of Congress on Thursday about immigration, asking why the American government would want to admit their citizens as immigrants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/13/world/americas/13trump-africa-print/13trump-africa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/13/world/americas/13trump-africa-print/13trump-africa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/13/world/americas/13trump-africa-print/13trump-africa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/13/world/americas/13trump-africa-print/13trump-a