, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c349134-895e-5e5c-85f5-6f23ce6a46b0', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c349134-895e-5e5c-85f5-6f23ce6a46b0'}, {'abstract': 'People from “holes” make America great, while Trump sinks into one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/12/opinion/proud-nation-of-holers.html', 'snippet': 'People from “holes” make America great, while Trump sinks into one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As tourist destinations go, the Republic of Moldova — tucked between Ukraine and Romania — probably isn’t on anyone’s bucket list. It’s the poorest country in Europe, with per capita G.D.P. barely exceeding Sudan’s. Sex trafficking and organized crime are rampant. My memories of the place, from a visit 17 years ago, include roads that vanished into deep snow, Transnistrian border guards in Soviet uniforms, and an impoverished Holocaust survivor’s tale of a bleak life under Romanian, German and Soviet tyrants.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/13/opinion/13Stephensweb/merlin_22230577_dc12b4fd-08a0-4f70-91b1-56158a05138b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 434, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/13/opinion/13Stephensweb/merlin_22230577_dc12b4fd-08a0-4f70-91b1-56158a05138b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 434}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/13/opinion/13Stephensweb/merlin_22230577_dc12b4fd-08a0-4f70-91b1-56158a05138b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/13/opinion/13Stephensweb/