rticle', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5131f04f-b71d-5da9-b93a-03491fc6e78f', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5131f04f-b71d-5da9-b93a-03491fc6e78f'}, {'abstract': 'The complete statement of the rape victim who was given an apology by a New York police official.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/12/nyregion/statement-from-victim-in-a-1994-brooklyn-rape-case.html', 'snippet': 'The complete statement of the rape victim who was given an apology by a New York police official.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, a senior New York police official apologized for sowing doubt in 1994 about the account of a woman who was raped in Prospect Park. Following is the statement the woman issued on Friday, shortly before the police official, John J. Miller, sent her his apology.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Statement From Victim in a 1994 Brooklyn Rape Case', 'kicker': 'A Request for an Apology', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Request for an Apology', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-01-13T01:38:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efe34217-56a3-5125-b19c-6a2a258ffe86', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efe34217-56a3-5125-b19c-6a2a258ffe86'}, {'abstract': 'Maybe he isn’t as unprecedented a leader as we think. All hail!', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/12/opinion/mr-president-your-toga-is-showing.html', 'snippet': 'Maybe he isn’t as unprecedented a leader as we think. All hail!', 'lead_paragra