pe': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Markham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd03b2a0-9f51-584f-b5f5-684c0feaa288', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd03b2a0-9f51-584f-b5f5-684c0feaa288'}, {'abstract': 'Neither the populists nor the philosophers are ready with alternatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/13/opinion/sunday/life-after-liberalism.html', 'snippet': 'Neither the populists nor the philosophers are ready with alternatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fourteen months ago, in the first flush of power, Steve Bannon gave an interview to Michael Wolff — beginning a relationship that would prove his undoing — in which he boasted about his plan to realign our politics. His nationalist-populist movement, he argued, would transform the G.O.P. into something truly new: a right-wing worker’s party that spent freely, “jacked up” infrastructure all over the country, and won “60 percent of the white vote” and “40 percent of the black and Hispanic vote” on its way to a 50-year majority.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/opinion/sunday/14douthat/merlin_132198047_55e94f65-15b8-46e3-b7b2-f202ad52727f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/16/opinion/sunday/14douthat/merlin_132198047_55e94f65-15b8-46e3-b7b2-f202ad52727f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 807}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/opinion/sunday/14douthat/merlin_132198047_55e94f65-15b8-46e3-b7b2-f202ad52727f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/opinion/sunday/14douthat/merlin_132198047_55e94f65-15b8-46e3-b7b2-f202ad52727f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1523, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/opinion/sunday/14douthat/14douthat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/16/opinion/sunday/14douthat/14douthat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/opinion/sunday/14douthat/14douthat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is There Life After Liberalism?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is There Life After Liberalism?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-13T19:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6072324-1270-5da5-b2d5-bd6a029b1f41', 'word_count': 836, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6072324-1270-5da5-b2d5-bd6a029b1f41'}, {'abstract': 'He has proposed increasing the nuclear arsenal and the ways in which it can be used, and is threatening the Iran deal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/13/opinion/sunday/trump-nuclear-weapons-war.html', 'snippet': 'He has proposed increasing the nuclear arsenal and the ways in which it can be used, and is threatening the Iran deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the sort of nightmare that had only ever been real for most people’s parents or grandparents — the fear of an impending nuclear attack. “Ballistic missile threat inbound to Hawaii,” read the emergency alert that residents of the Aloha State received on Saturday morning. “Seek immediate shelter. This is not a drill.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14sun1/14sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14sun1/14sun1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14sun1/14sun1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14sun1/14sun1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1196, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/14/opinion/14sun1/14sun1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy':