dren and Childhood', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-15T10:30:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron E. Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71ba70f6-05c6-55b4-9606-72ee50f21593', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71ba70f6-05c6-55b4-9606-72ee50f21593'}, {'abstract': 'During an epidemic, self-delusion won’t reduce the viral load.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/15/opinion/happy-flu-year.html', 'snippet': 'During an epidemic, self-delusion won’t reduce the viral load.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — In a flash of New Year’s optimism, you write a hopeful essay, and since you’re all in for hope, you invest in three pounds of collard greens and the thickest pork chops at the store, plus a pile of black-eyed peas, for a special supper on New Year’s Day. You don’t even care for collard greens or pork chops or black-eyed peas, but in the American South this is luck-producing food. The president of the United States is engaged in a war of insults with a nuclear-armed enemy, and this is no time to take a chance with luck.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15renklWeb/15renklWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15renklWeb/15renklWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 746}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15renklWeb/15renklWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15renklWeb/15renklWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1965, 'width': 1581, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15renklWeb/15renklWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15renklWeb/15renklWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15renklWeb/15renklWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Flu Year!', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New Year', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-15T10:45:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Renkl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Renkl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcdf0943-2261-5fbd-9f57-109b0ee9a4a2', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcdf0943-2261-5fbd-9f57-109b0ee9a4a2'}, {'abstract': 'Our greatest civil rights leader was clear: Those who remain silent will also stand accused.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/15/opinion/martin-luther-king-trump-racism.html', 'snippet': 'Our greatest civil rights leader was clear: Those who remain silent will also stand accused.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s come clean: President Trump is a white racist! Over the past few days, many have written, spoken and shouted this fact, but it needs repeating: President Trump is a white racist! Why repeat it? Because many have been under the grand illusion that America is a “post-racial” nation, a beautiful melting pot where racism is only sporadic, infrequent and expressed by those on the margins of an otherwise mainstream and “decent” America. That’s a lie; a blatant one at that. We must face a very horrible truth. And America is so cowardly when it comes to facing awful truths about itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15yancyWeb/15yancyWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15yancyWeb/15yancyWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15yancyWeb/15yancyWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15yancyWeb/15yancyWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1525, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15yancyWeb/15yancyWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/15/opinion/15yancyWeb/15yancyWeb-thumbStandard.