kitchens, will host a vegetarian dinner in February at the James Beard Foundation. Rachana Rimal, one of the league’s instructors, will cook the Nepali menu. Cheese-filled spinach croquettes, cauliflower fried in chickpea batter, and black dal served with mustard greens, roasted eggplant, basmati rice and pickles are among the items planned. An Uzbek dinner, which will be the first halal meal at the Beard House, is planned for May: Nepalese Vegetarian Feast, Feb. 2 at 7 p.m., $135 for members, $175 for nonmembers, James Beard Foundation, 167 West 12th Street (Seventh Avenue), jamesbeard.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerdinner/merlin_131866763_968bf955-9be2-4e06-95cc-c8a711d6be37-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerdinner/merlin_131866763_968bf955-9be2-4e06-95cc-c8a711d6be37-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerdinner/merlin_131866763_968bf955-9be2-4e06-95cc-c8a711d6be37-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerdinner/merlin_131866763_968bf955-9be2-4e06-95cc-c8a711d6be37-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerdinner/17burnerkitchen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'