: 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f620fb5-c7d9-5550-84a3-44a2cfcaad25', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f620fb5-c7d9-5550-84a3-44a2cfcaad25'}, {'abstract': 'Two masked teenagers broke into a fourth-grade classroom in Perm, the latest in a series of assaults that have prompted a debate about school security.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/15/world/europe/russia-perm-school-attack.html', 'snippet': 'Two masked teenagers broke into a fourth-grade classroom in Perm, the latest in a series of assaults that have prompted a debate about school security.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Two masked teenagers armed with knives stormed a school in the central Russian city of Perm on Monday, wounding at least 12 people, most of them elementary school students.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/world/16Russia/merlin_132303944_d091913c-8992-4b56-a701-e14ad44d0019-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/16/world/16Russia/merlin_132303944_d091913c-8992-4b56-a701-e14ad44d0019-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/world/16Russia/merlin_132303944_d091913c-8992-4b56-a701-e14ad44d0019-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/world/16Russia/merlin_132303944_d091913c-8992-4b56-a701-e14ad44d0019-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/world/16Russia/16Russia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/16/world/16Russia/16Russia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/16/world/16Russia/16Russia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knife Attack at Russian School Leaves at Least 12 Wounded', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings and Armed Attacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Perm (Russia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbine High School', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-15T17:20:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Luxmoore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Luxmoore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19cda5ea-8b9e-50d7-9070-07597ae85da5', 'word_count': 574, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19cda5ea-8b9e-50d7-9070-07597ae85da5'}, {'abstract': 'A new book explores the food passions and larder of a founding father.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/15/dining/stirring-the-pot-with-benjamin-franklin-book.html', 'snippet': 'A new book explores the food passions and larder of a founding father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new book about Benjamin Franklin covers his 84 years and the food that accompanied them, all based on prodigious research by Rae Katherine Eighmey, a food historian. The account is dense with detail, conveying Mr. Franklin’s tastes, curiosity and inventiveness, including kitchen innovations like a special oven. Recipes for vegetables and salads (including a warm one dressed with melted butter and verjus) may come as a surprise to some readers. Ledgers kept by his French household manager illustrate the range of products in his kitchen, including vanilla beans, artichokes and ingredients for ice cream. Worth trying is an apple tart made with applesauce custard: “Stirring the Pot With Benjamin Franklin: A Founding Father’s Culinary Adventures” by Rae Katherine Eighmey (Smithsonian Books, $21.95).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerbook/merlin_132031106_b7ca59f0-f6dc-4197-ba9e-122dc92d48d1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerbook/merlin_132031106_b7ca59f0-f6dc-4197-ba9e-122dc92d48d1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 853}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerbook/merlin_132031106_b7ca59f0-f6dc-4197-ba9e-122dc92d48d1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 720, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerbook/merlin_132031106_b7ca59f0-f6dc-4197-ba9e-122dc92d48d1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1440, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerbook/17burnerbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerbook/17burnerbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burnerbook/17burnerbook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cooking, the Benjamin Franklin Way', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Head: Benjamin Franklin’s  Way to Cook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eighmey, Rae Katherine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Benjamin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Stirring the Pot With Benjamin Franklin: A Founding Father's Culinary Adventures (Book)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-15T17:24:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50de22ca-9d54-563c-9af9-42fd710d0aaf', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50de22ca-9d54-563c-9af9-42fd710d0aaf'}, {'abstract': 'Find a selection of briny favorites from the coasts at the Lobster Place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/15/dining/oysters-canada-pink-moon-beau-soleil.html', 'snippet': 'Find a selection of briny favorites from the coasts at the Lobster Place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cold waters off Canada’s east and west coasts produce some excellent oysters. For years, the enjoyable briny-sweet Malpeque from Prince Edward Island has been the best-known and most widely available in the United States. But there are others vying for popularity. Pink Moons, also from Prince Edward Island, are richly briny. The somewhat smaller, slightly nutty-tasting Beau Soleil from New Brunswick is a favorite of mine. Fanny Bays from the West Coast of Canada offer mellow flavor touched with salt: Lobster Place, Chelsea Market, 75 Ninth Avenue (15th Street), 212-255-5672, lobsterplace.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burneroyster/17burneroyster-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burneroyster/17burneroyster-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burneroyster/17burneroyster-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burneroyster/17burneroyster-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1294, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burneroyster/17burneroyster-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burneroyster/17burneroyster-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/dining/17burneroyster/17burneroyster-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada’s Oysters: Treasures Ready to Be Slurped', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Shuck: Treasures Ready To Be Slurped', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oysters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chelsea Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Brunswick (Canada)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prince Edward Island (Canada)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-15T17:27:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb667906-ef59-580a-ac47-11302a9df655', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb667906-ef59-580a-ac47-11302a9df655'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. O’Riordan’s voice, high and breathy but more determined than fragile, lent an unmistakable sound to songs like the hits “Linger” and “Zombie.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/15/obituaries/dolores-oriordan-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. O’Riordan’s voice, high and breathy but more determined than fragile, lent an unmistakable sound to songs like the hits “Linger” and “Zombie.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dolores O’Riordan, the lead singer of the Irish rock band the Cranberries, died on Monday in London. She was 46.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dolores O’Riordan, Lead Singer of the Cranberries, Dies at 46', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dolores O’Riordan, Cranberries Lead Singer, Dies at 46', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Riordan, Dolores", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cranberries, The (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-15T18:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/0aa60793-2138-52f9-bc86-deee32b2da4d', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0aa60793-2138-52f9-bc86-deee32b2da4d'}, {'abstract': 'Miuccia Prada recast her history of nylon. Silvia Venturini Fendi made the world a luggage pickup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/15/fashion/prada-fendi-milan.html', 'snippet': 'Miuccia Prada recast her history of nylon. Silvia Venturini Fendi made the world a luggage pickup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — Founded here in 1913 as a luggage purveyor to the local carriage trade, Fratelli Prada probably would not have become a synonym for Italian fashion had the male scion, uninterested in the business, not passed it on to his daughter, Luisa, who in turn eventually handed the baton to a daughter of her o