 new version is byAlexei Ratmansky.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/16/arts/dance/bolshoi-ballet-alexei-ratmansky-romeo-and-juliet-.html', 'snippet': 'The Bolshoi contains multitudes — or, at least, doubles of some repertory, including “Romeo and Juliet,” whose new version is byAlexei Ratmansky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The Bolshoi Theater is a behemoth, an immense cafe-au-lait colored columned structure that fills a city block across from Red Square here. Since 2002, it has been complemented by a second, smaller theater just up the hill. Those theaters house the largest — and possibly the most contentious — ballet company in the world, a place of titanic personalities and deep history. (It is here that Sergei Filin, then director of the company, had a jar of battery acid flung in his face in 2013.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/arts/17romeojuliet/17romeojuliet-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/17/arts/17romeojuliet/17romeojuliet-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/arts/17romeojuliet/17romeojuliet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/arts/17romeojuliet/17romeojuliet-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/arts/17romeojuliet/17romeojuliet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': '