'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99a6e788-20db-5323-aa75-08757c4c94cc', 'word_count': 796, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99a6e788-20db-5323-aa75-08757c4c94cc'}, {'abstract': 'The second installment of FX’s “American Crime Story” series is occasionally about Mr. Versace, but is more focused on his murderer, Andrew Cunanan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/16/arts/television/the-assassination-of-gianni-versace-review.html', 'snippet': 'The second installment of FX’s “American Crime Story” series is occasionally about Mr. Versace, but is more focused on his murderer, Andrew Cunanan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At some point we’ll all have to grapple with the idea that the warped compassion of the modern true-crime boom implicates its audience and that viewers are greedily lining up to be part of a lurid long tail of suffering and despair. If “The Assassination of Gianni Versace: American Crime Story” were a little more interesting, maybe it would be that lightning rod. But instead it’s a surprisingly inert, if lushly imagined, tale.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18versace2/17VERSACE-print-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18versace2/17VERSACE-print-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18versace2/17VERSACE-print-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18versace2/17VERSACE-print-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18versace2/17VERSACE-print-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18versace2/17VERSACE-print-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18versace2/17VERSACE-print-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘The Assassination of Gianni Versace’ Is Fashionable, but Flat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Making of a Murderer, Confusingly Told', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Assassination of Gianni Versace: American Crime Story (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FX (TV Network)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Criss, Darren', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Versace, Gianni', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunanan, Andrew Phillip', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Ryan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_