york-new-jersey-mob.html', 'snippet': 'The survival of the Waterfront Commission of New York Harbor, whose 65-year mission has been to root out corruption, is threatened by a New Jersey law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After 65 years of battling against the influence of organized crime on the docks, the Waterfront Commission of New York Harbor is fighting for its own survival. Its biggest threat has come not from the mob in Brooklyn or Bayonne, N.J., but from elected officials in Trenton.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/nyregion/18waterfront1/merlin_132408647_07adad5c-4e30-43ca-b179-352511a3c21a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/18/nyregion/18waterfront1/merlin_132408647_07adad5c-4e30-43ca-b179-352511a3c21a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/nyregion/18waterfront1/merlin_132408647_07adad5c-4e30-43ca-b179-352511a3c21a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/nyregion/18waterfront1/merlin_132408647_07adad5c-4e30-43ca-b179-352511a3c21a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/nyregion/18waterfront1/merlin_132408647_07adad5c-4e30-43ca-b179-352511a3c21a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/18/nyregion/18waterfront1/merlin_132408647_07adad5c-4e30-43ca-b179-352511a3c21a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/nyregion/18waterfront1/merlin_132408647_07adad5c-4e30-43ca-b179-352511a3c21a-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Waterfront, a Mob Watchdog Is Fighting to Survive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mob Watchdog Fights Trenton to Stay on the Waterfront', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Waterfront Commission of New York Harbor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racketeering and Racketeers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "International Longshoremen's Assn", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Shipping Assn', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lesniak, Raymond J', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-17T17:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/077c6044-5936-5a41-a46d-a00e906de1b6', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/077c6044-5936-5a41-a46d-a00e906de1b6'}, {'abstract': 'There is no shortage of history, sultry beauty and architectural delights. And a visit needn’t cost you much.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/17/travel/savannah-georgia-budget.html', 'snippet': 'There is no shortage of history, sultry beauty and architectural delights. And a visit needn’t cost you much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My guide, Karen Wortham, led me on a path from Johnson Square, one of the many quadrangular parks that give Savannah, Ga., its distinct character, down to River Street, which runs along the Savannah River. We stopped in front of a relatively modest statue that depicted a black family with an inscription from Maya Angelou below. The statue, Ms. Wortham explained, was a compromise after a yearslong battle with the city. Originally, she said, the monument was to depict a more real, raw picture of slavery in Georgia. The city balked, and the monument’s designer settled on a family of four in church clothes, with chains lying at the family’s feet. The quotation, too, was called into question for its graphic language, but it was, Ms. Wortham said, simply the reality of what happened.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/17/travel/17frugal-savannah/merlin_131685140_16acb4cd-986d-40ea-8de7-58e32a4bea30-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/17/travel/17frugal-savannah/merlin_131685140_16acb4cd-986d-40ea-8de7-58e32a4bea30-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {