ps://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/17/movies/sundance-film-festival-preview.html', 'snippet': 'The festival starts Thursday. Here’s a look at five films we’re excited about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as the movie business continues to shift its models, the Sundance Film Festival remains a place where careers are born, Oscar dreams arise and top-dollar distribution deals are made. This year’s edition starts Thursday, Jan. 18, in Park City, Utah and runs through Jan. 28. Here are five movies we’re looking forward to that could make an impact.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/movies/18sundance1/18sundance1-articleLarge-v3.png', 'height': 298, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/18/movies/18sundance1/18sundance1-articleLarge-v3.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 298}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/movies/18sundance1/18sundance1-jumbo-v3.png', 'height': 447, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/movies/18sundance1/18sundance1-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 447, 'width': 899, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/movies/18sundance1/18sundance1-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/18/movies/18sundance1/18sundance1-thumbStandard-v3.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/movies/18sundance1/18sundance1-thumbLarge-v3.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sundance Film Festival: 5 Movies to Watch', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Spirit of Sundance, Packing a Punch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akhavan, Desiree', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dano, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moretz, Chloe Grace', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammer, Armie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Tessa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oxenbould, Ed', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Sorry to Bother You (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Leave No Trace (Movie)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hereditary (Movie)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Wildlife (Movie)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Miseducation of Cameron Post (Movie)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-17T18:31:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a87012b7-50b6-5916-973b-4c50a79d6346', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a87012b7-50b6-5916-973b-4c50a79d6346'}, {'abstract': 'After years writing songs for Lady Antebellum and Meghan Trainor, among others, the 31-year-old shows off her own striking voice on her major-label debut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/17/arts/music/caitlyn-smith-starfire-review.html', 'snippet': 'After years writing songs for Lady Antebellum and Meghan Trainor, among others, the 31-year-old shows off her own striking voice on her major-label debut.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I scream my lungs out/Confess my secrets, all my sins,” Caitlyn Smith sings on “Starfire,” her first major-label album after three early efforts in her teens. “But they don’t give a damn/’Cause if it don’t sound like the radio — pass.” The song is called “This Town Is Killing Me,” and she does name the town: It’s Nashville.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18album-smit/18album-smith1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 471, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18album-smit/18album-smith1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 471}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18album-smit/18album-smith1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 803, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18album-smit/18album-smith1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1607, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18album-smit/18album-smith1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18album-smit/18album-smith1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/18/arts/18album-smit/18album-smith1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Caitlyn Smith, a Hitmaking Nashville Songwriter, Sings Her Own on ‘Starfire’', 'kicker': 'Album Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hit-Making Songwriter Steps Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Caitlyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Starfire (Album)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-17T18:41:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2588ade8-4dc1-50ea-9dc8-a3fbcd797a4a', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2588ade8-4dc1-50ea-9dc8-a3fbcd797a4a'}, {'abstract': 'John Hawkes stars as a hard-boozing former cop who stumbles into a mystery involving some very young women and some very bad men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/17/movies/small-town-crime-review-john-hawkes.html', 'snippet': 'John Hawkes stars as a hard-boozing former cop who stumbles into a mystery involving some very young women and some very bad men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A genre exercise, the detective movie “Small Town Crime” relies on the usual time-tested ingredients: the boozy loner lawman, the beautiful female victim and the reliably mysterious, invariably competent villains. The directors and brothers Eshom Nelms and Ian Nelms have obviously made a study of the genre, both in its old and more recent iterations, and while they’re happy to play around with the form, they pretty much leave the basics intact. By far their smartest, most inspired move is to have cleared room for John Hawkes, one of those actors who are more often seen nibbling at the edges of a scene, leaving perfect little teeth marks that sometimes give a movie its primary texture.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/arts/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/19/arts/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/arts/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/arts/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/arts/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/19/arts/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562/19smalltowncrime-1516142217562-thumbStandard.jpg', 