': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/18/books/president-trump-book-list.html', 'snippet': 'Here are books the president has tweeted about since taking office in 2017.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year into the Trump administration, Americans have a pretty good idea what the president has been watching on TV during his time in office, largely thanks to his active Twitter feed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/books/review/19TRUMPBOOK-image/merlin_131896049_46bd29e3-5569-467d-91df-f7a09bac3b2c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/19/books/review/19TRUMPBOOK-image/merlin_131896049_46bd29e3-5569-467d-91df-f7a09bac3b2c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/books/review/19TRUMPBOOK-image/merlin_131896049_46bd29e3-5569-467d-91df-f7a09bac3b2c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/books/review/19TRUMPBOOK-image/merlin_131896049_46bd29e3-5569-467d-91df-f7a09bac3b2c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1376, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/books/review/19TRUMPBOOK-image/merlin_131896049_46bd29e3-5569-467d-91df-f7a09bac3b2c-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/19/books/review/19TRUMPBOOK-image/merlin_131896049_46bd29e3-5569-467d-91df-f7a09bac3b2c-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/books/review/19TRUMPBOOK-image/merlin_131896049_46bd29e3-5569-467d-91df-f7a09bac3b2c-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Sat on Trump’s Nightstand This Year?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-18T19:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Ellingwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ellingwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a700967-90d3-5e5e-8a01-ade7186dc096', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a700967-90d3-5e5e-8a01-ade7186dc096'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/18/books/review/new-noteworthy-choire-sicha.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of books published this week; plus, a peek at what our colleagues around the newsroom are reading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SO YOU WANT TO TALK ABOUT RACE By Ijeoma Oluo. (Seal Press, $27.) Oluo takes on the thorniest questions surrounding race, from police brutality to who can use the “N” word. One chapter even has this intriguing heading: “I Just Got Called a Racist, What Do I Do Now?” ANGELITOS By Ilan Stavans and Santiago Cohen. (Mad Creek Books, $17.95.) This graphic novel has a simple, gritty style. It tells the story of Padre Chinchachoma, a Catholic priest known on the streets of Mexico City as a protector of homeless children who raised the ire of the local police and was suspected of sexual abuse. CULTURE AS WEAPON By Nato Thompson. (Melville House, $24.99.) Thompson is an art curator and activist who has a problem with the way that corporations have co-opted the realm of culture to ensure profits, shape public opinion and control dissent. IT OCCURS TO ME THAT I AM AMERICA Edited by Jonathan Santlofer. (Touchstone, $30.) Timed to the first anniversary of Donald Trump’s inauguration, this collection packs in an impressive array of fiction writers and illustrators. The likes of Joyce Carol Oates, Neil Gaiman and Art Spiegelman assert their own visions for a democratic society. NIKOLAI GOGOL By Vladimir Nabokov. (New Directions, $16.95.) In Nabokov’s classic biography of the Russian novelist, newly reissued, he begins with Gogol’s death and works back to his birth. Nabokov is particularly good at capturing the humorist in Gogol, a writer often misinterpreted as a kind of Russian Dickens.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/books/review/21NewNoteworthy1/21NewNoteworthy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 278, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/12/books/review/21NewNoteworthy1/21NewNoteworthy1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 278}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/books/review/21NewNoteworthy1/21NewNoteworthy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 474, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/12/books/review/21NewNoteworthy1/2