eadline': 'Your Evening Briefing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-01-18T23:10:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Zraick and Sandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zraick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/68ecc929-0dca-5854-b57f-1e9771b21b31', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68ecc929-0dca-5854-b57f-1e9771b21b31'}, {'abstract': 'We are living in a high moment for feminism, but we all reveal our implicit biases through the internet every day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/18/nyregion/metoo-and-the-marketing-of-female-narrative.html', 'snippet': 'We are living in a high moment for feminism, but we all reveal our implicit biases through the internet every day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Monday, Mathilde Krim died. She was a biologist who spoke five languages; who contributed, in her 20s and 30s, to more than a dozen papers on cancer and virology; ran the interferon lab at Memorial Sloan Kettering; served on a team that developed a method for determining sex in utero; smuggled guns to opponents of British rule in Palestine; threw John F. Kennedy’s 45th-birthday party at her East Side townhouse; married twice, had a daughter and later received the Presidential Medal of Freedom for her historic work in AIDS research and advocacy. At the news of her death, the internet paid relatively little attention.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/nyregion/21big/merlin_42443920_7edcfd91-0a1f-4920-bd6b-62a250a613a4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/21/nyregion/21big/merlin_42443920_7edcfd91-0a1f-4920-bd6b-62a250a613a4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/nyregion/21big/merlin_42443920_7edcfd91-0a1f-4920-bd6b-62a250a613a4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/nyregion/21big/merlin_42443920_7edcfd91-0a1f-4920-bd6b-62a250a613a4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/nyregion/21big/21big-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/21/nyregion/21big/21big-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/nyregion/21big/21big-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '#MeToo and the Marketing of Female Narrative', 'kicker': 'Big City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On the Internet, Our Biases Show', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krim, Mathilde', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '#MeToo Movement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Socia