bstract': 'Berlin may be the most musically active city on earth. It’s also at a moment of transition, with a fresh crop of artistic leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/19/arts/music/berlin-classical-music-young-leaders.html', 'snippet': 'Berlin may be the most musically active city on earth. It’s also at a moment of transition, with a fresh crop of artistic leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With three full-time opera houses, seven major symphony orchestras and numerous world-class choirs, all lavishly funded by the German government, Berlin may well be the most musically active city on earth. It has also reached a moment of transition, with the rise of a new generation of young, international musical chiefs. While Daniel Barenboim, 75, remains the dean of the Berlin music scene, and another veteran, 77-year-old Christoph Eschenbach, arrives in 2019 to lead the Konzerthausorchester, many older maestros are passing the baton to a new crop of musical leaders. Here’s a look at several of the new arrivals injecting vitality into an already thriving landscape.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/arts/21BERLINMUSIC-COMBO/21BERLINMUSIC-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/21/arts/21BERLINMUSIC-COMBO/21BERLINMUSIC-COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/arts/21BERLINMUSIC-COMBO/21BERLINMUSIC-COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/arts/21BERLINMUSIC-COMBO/21BERLINMUSIC-COMBO-superJumbo.j