me': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubikis, Ainars', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Souza, Jordan', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schulz, Matthias', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Staatsoper', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Staatsoper Unter den Linden', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-19T16:06:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.J. Goldmann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Goldmann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57808648-6b02-5327-a66b-dd02f3477a3c', 'word_count': 1546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57808648-6b02-5327-a66b-dd02f3477a3c'}, {'abstract': 'Forget the sophomore slump — Chloe Benjamin’s second novel, “The Immortalists,” has rocketed to No. 7 in its first week on sale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/19/books/review/chloe-benjamin-the-immortalists-best-sellers.html', 'snippet': 'Forget the sophomore slump — Chloe Benjamin’s second novel, “The Immortalists,” has rocketed to No. 7 in its first week on sale.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BURNING QUESTION: Would you want to know the date of your death? That’s the premise of Chloe Benjamin’s captivating family saga “The Immortalists,” which enters the hardcover fiction list at No. 7. It begins in the late 1960s, when all four Gold children — at loose ends on Manhattan’s Lower East Side during a steamy, sticky summer vacation — decide to visit a fortuneteller famous for predicting when people will die. As Benjamin, 29, explained in an interview with NPR, “the novel follows each of the siblings over about 50 years as they reckon with their prophecies. Some of them fight against it. Others claim they don’t believe in it. Some use it to push them to pursue their wildest dreams. And others are surprisingly limited by it even if their date of death is quite far out.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/books/review/0128-BKS-LIST/0128-BKS-LIST-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 609, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/28/books/review/0128-BKS-LIST/0128-BKS-LIST-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 609}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/books/review/0128-BKS-LIST/0128-BKS-LIST-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 824, 'width': 812, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/books/review/0128-BKS-LIST/0128-BKS-LIST-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 824, 'width': 812, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/books/review/0128-BKS-LIST/0128-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/28/books/review/0128-BKS-LIST/0128-BKS-LIST-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/books/review/0128-BKS-LIST/0128-BKS-LIST-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Young Novelist Grapples With Matters of Life and Death', 'k