, 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21nguyen/21nguyen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21nguyen/21nguyen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What I’ve Learned from My 4-Year-Old', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Learning To Listen  From My Son', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnamese-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-20T19:30:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Viet Thanh Nguyen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viet', 'middlename': 'Thanh', 'lastname': 'Nguyen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4aa3f40-927c-50d2-a554-ffc7aeb8d1f3', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4aa3f40-927c-50d2-a554-ffc7aeb8d1f3'}, {'abstract': 'In shattering comforting fictions about how things work in America, he’s made us face our country’s lack of decency and shame. Finally.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/20/opinion/sunday/donald-trump-political-mythbuster.html', 'snippet': 'In shattering comforting fictions about how things work in America, he’s made us face our country’s lack of decency and shame. Finally.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Trump prides himself on destruction. He smashes conceptions and breaks traditions. In doing so without suffering any significant consequences, he has made it more difficult for Americans to continue to delude ourselves with fairy tales about our collective values and to indulge in comforting fictions about the fundamental decency of our politics.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21smith-WEB/21smith-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 514, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21smith-WEB/21smith-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 514}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21smith-WEB/21smith-WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 877, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21smith-WEB/21smith-WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1058, 'width': 1235, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21smith-WEB/21smith-WEB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21smith-WEB/21smith-WEB-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21smith-WEB/21smith-WEB-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Political Mythbuster in Chief', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Political Mythbuster in Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-20T19:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamil Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d6338d9-48ef-54d4-ba1f-1d963f21280b', 'word_count': 1046, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d6338d9-48ef-54d4-ba1f-1d963f21280b'}, {'abstract': 'I’ve had a year of deep disagreement very close to home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/20/opinion/sunday/a-trump-size-hole-in-our-relationship.html', 'snippet': 'I’ve had a year of deep disagreement very close to home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This must be what it feels like to be the victim of a random attack: shock, disbelief, disorientation, confusion, distress. But I’m aware that I was not a target. I’m just in the wrong time in America.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21abercrombie/21abercrombie-articleLarge.jpg', 'height':