y', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abercrombie-Winstanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3e98e1c-6272-57ae-999f-317c5670bf1d', 'word_count': 1488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3e98e1c-6272-57ae-999f-317c5670bf1d'}, {'abstract': 'The best way to evaluate President Trump’s first year in office is to compare him not with the great presidents but with the worst.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/20/opinion/sunday/trump-bad-presidents-history.html', 'snippet': 'The best way to evaluate President Trump’s first year in office is to compare him not with the great presidents but with the worst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Historians have long looked to a few key criteria in evaluating the beginning of a president’s administration. First and foremost, any new president should execute public duties with a commanding civility and poise befitting the nation’s chief executive, but without appearing aloof or haughty. As George Washington observed at the outset of his presidency in 1789, the president cannot in any way “demean himself in his public character” and must act “in such a manner as to maintain the dignity of office.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21wilentz/21wilentz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21wilentz/21wilentz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21wilentz/21wilentz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21wilentz/21wilentz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1115, 'width': 1670, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21wilentz/21wilentz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21wilentz/21wilentz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/21/opinion/sunday/21wilentz/21wilentz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'They Were Bad. He May Be Worse.', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They Were Bad. He May Be Worse.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buchanan, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fillmore, Millard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harding, Warren G', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Andrew', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierce, Franklin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-20T19:39:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sean Wilentz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilentz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ba2de78-8f55-5219-a0be-6a3f1e3200b9', 'word_count': 1342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ba2de78-8f55-5219-a0be-6a3f1e3200b9'}, {'abstract': 'What life has been like as an imam during Donald Trump’s first year in office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/20/opinion/sunday/islam-lessons-trump.html', 'snippet': 'What life has been like as an imam during Donald Trump’s first year in office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANAHEIM, Calif. — Donald Trump’s inauguration took place on a Friday, the weekly holy day for Muslims. I’d been dreading it: We would have a new president, one who had threatened to shut down mosques and bar Muslims from entering the country. I knew I had to say something to make people feel better about it.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/23/opinion/sunday/21umar/merlin_132423542_8a6a642a-af20-4981-9edc-8a3736474e1d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/23/opinion/sunday/21umar/merlin_132423542_8a6a642a-af20-4981-9edc-8a3736474e1d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/23/opinion/sunday/21umar/merlin_132423542_8a6a642a-af20-4981-9edc-8a3736474e1d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima