 Roosevelt and Ernest Hemingway on safari.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harry Selby, one of the last of Africa’s renowned white hunters, who took rich and famous safari clients into the interiors of Kenya, Tanganyika and Botswana for a half-century to shoot game, photograph exotic wildlife and search for elusive adventure in the bush, died on Saturday at his home in Maun, Botswana. He was 92.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/us/22selby1/merlin_132594593_b5037f12-658c-41f0-b3c2-4b8bfb7298c2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 630, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/22/us/22selby1/merlin_132594593_b5037f12-658c-41f0-b3c2-4b8bfb7298c2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 630}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/us/22selby1/merlin_132594593_b5037f12-658c-41f0-b3c2-4b8bfb7298c2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 976, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/us/22selby1/merlin_132594593_b5037f12-658c-41f0-b3c2-4b8bfb7298c2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1951, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/us/22selby1/22selby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/22/us/22selby1/22selby-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/us/22selby1/22selby-thumbLarge.jpg', '