inal': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb5b3899-ec16-5262-b138-25e61e5a38f2', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb5b3899-ec16-5262-b138-25e61e5a38f2'}, {'abstract': 'The last time a Hispanic actor was nominated for an Academy Award was 2012 and, according to a study, only 3 percent of speaking characters in films are Latino.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/21/business/media/hollywood-diversity-hispanics.html', 'snippet': 'The last time a Hispanic actor was nominated for an Academy Award was 2012 and, according to a study, only 3 percent of speaking characters in films are Latino.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — After black actors and films that focused on black characters were overlooked for Oscar nominations in 2015 and 2016, the #OscarsSoWhite social media outcry was so fierce that Hollywood was forced to listen. The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences began a determined diversification effort, and last year there were six black acting nominees, a record.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/business/media/hispanics-oscars-grid-1516406035742/hispanics-oscars-grid-1516406035742-jumbo.png', 'height': 226, 'width': 533, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/business/media/hispanics-oscars-grid-1516406035742/hispanics-oscars-grid-1516406035742-superJumbo.png', 'height': 226, 'width': 533, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/19/business/media/hispanics-oscars-grid-1516406035742/hispanics-oscars-grid-1516406035742-thumb