Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "State Children's Health Insurance Program (S-CHIP)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (2017)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-22T20:27:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margot Sanger-Katz and Jim Tankersley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanger-Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tankersley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaaea6fa-52bb-536d-9fd5-280104f49a48', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaaea6fa-52bb-536d-9fd5-280104f49a48'}, {'abstract': 'Shutdowns and stopgaps are no way to deal with the Dreamers or any other aspect of our immigration policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/22/opinion/government-shutdown-stopgap-dreamers.html', 'snippet': 'Shutdowns and stopgaps are no way to deal with the Dreamers or any other aspect of our immigration policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bret Stephens: Gail, over the past few days, it’s been the battle of the shutdown hashtags. If you’re a Republican, it was the #SchumerShutdown. If you’re a Democrat, it was the #TrumpShutdown. I suspect that, for most Americans, the appropriate hashtag is #WhatIsWrongWithThesePeople? Now the Senate has voted to reopen the government, at least for a few weeks, and presumably the House will follow any minute. Give me your thoughts on shutdown politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22conversation2-web/merlin_132600677_1156c0e1-376e-4771-87af-5c2573029ee2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22conversation2-web/merlin_132600677_1156c0e1-376e-4771-87af-5c2573029ee2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22conversation2-web/merlin_132600677_1156c0e1-376e-4771-87af-5c2573029ee2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22conversation2-web/merlin_132600677_1156c0e1-376e-4771-87af-5c2573029ee2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22conversation2-web/22conversation2-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22conversation2-web/22conversation2-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22conversation2-web/22conversation2-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Government Is Dead. Long Live the Government!', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_