ll city in Wisconsin, which has a well-regarded state university system that an overwhelming majority of my peers expected to and did attend. The promise of that university education was why the people I grew up with believed in the dream.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22cauleyWeb/22cauleyWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22cauleyWeb/22cauleyWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22cauleyWeb/22cauleyWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22cauleyWeb/22cauleyWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22cauleyWeb/22cauleyWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22cauleyWeb/22cauleyWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/22/opinion/22cauleyWeb/22cauleyWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Is Killing the American Dream', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-22T21:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kashana Cauley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kashana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cauley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f4f13d7-3758-556e-b986-836a8ebfceb6', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f4f13d7-3758-556e-b986-836a8ebfceb6'}, {'abstract': 'The dessert shop on East Broadway is a project from two Dominique Ansel and La Sirena alums.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/22/dining/little-one-dessert-shop.html', 'snippet': 'The dessert shop on East Broadway is a project from two Dominique Ansel and La Sirena alums.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a new, serene little respite from a busy stretch of East Broadway, the attraction is a collection of desserts, mostly Japanese for now, to eat in or take away. The chefs Eddie Zheng and Olivia Leung — both graduates of the Institute of Culinary Education, with credentials from places like Dominique Ansel and La Sirena — offer monaka ice cream sandwiches in flavors like buckwheat and corn encased in crisp shells. Tidy dorayaki honey pancakes have fillings that include matcha cream and seared banana, and apple confit with mascarpone. They’re just getting going, Mr. Zheng said, and they expect to add more desserts soon: The Little One, 150 East Broadway (Rutgers Street), no phone, no website.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/dining/24bur