 the same time the daguerreotype enjoyed a similar surge in popularity. Some of the images evoke a certain Brooklyn demographic.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2018/01/23/the-age-of-gold-rush-and-daguerreotypes/', 'snippet': 'A collection of images showcases the intensity of the Gold Rush in the 19th century, around the same time the daguerreotype enjoyed a similar surge in popularity. Some of the images evoke a certain Brooklyn demographic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographic process may depend on silver, but a new exhibit shows how gold — specifically, its discovery in California 170 years ago this week — was just as important as a subject for daguerreotypes. During the later half of the 19th century, gold fever was as intense — and short lived — as the nascent photographic process.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Age of Gold and Daguerreotypes', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Louis-Jacques-Mandé Daguerre', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luce Lebart', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daguerre, Louis (1787-1851)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lebart, Luce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Gallery of Canada', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-23T09:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Moroz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moroz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organi