e-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sea of Trash on Lebanon’s Beaches', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sea of Garbage Covers the Beaches Of Lebanon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'vis-multimedia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beirut (Lebanon)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mediterranean Sea', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-23T22:34:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nada Homsi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nada', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Homsi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a1c0422-b96e-50eb-bf6a-1abad64fd7af', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a1c0422-b96e-50eb-bf6a-1abad64fd7af'}, {'abstract': 'Not being able to watch a football game is a problem. But not having a strategy is a bigger problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/23/magazine/congress-suddenly-cares-about-the-troops-when-a-shutdown-looms-what-about-the-rest-of-the-time.html', 'snippet': 'Not being able to watch a football game is a problem. But not having a strategy is a bigger problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the United States government last shut down over a congressional impasse, in 2013, I was 20 days shy of my discharge from the Marine Corps, in Camp Pendleton, Calif. A last-minute bill, signed the day before the rest of the federal government’s appropriations were set to expire, guaranteed that I and the rest of the military would continue to receive our paychecks. It was comforting, I suppose, to know that at least Congress could muster the bipartisan will to accomplish something, but even at the time it struck me as absurd: The same Congress and administration that jumped at the opportunity to demonstrate how much they cared about the troops seemed perfectly comfortable with the status quo of endless war. Missing a paycheck would have been an inconvenience. Fighting in a war that I still don’t understand, however, has affected me and my brothers and sisters in uniform in far more pernicious and long-lasting ways.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/23/magazine/23mag-shutdown2/23mag-shutdown2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/23/magazine/23mag-shutdown2/23mag-shutdown2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/23/magazine/23mag-shutdown2/23mag-shutdown2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/23/magazine/23mag-shutdown2/23mag-shutdown2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/23/magazine/23mag-shutdown2/23mag-shutdown2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/23/magazine/23mag-shutdown2/23mag-shutdown2-thumbStandard.jpg'