ness that evoked the humor and absurdity of modern life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/23/obituaries/nicanor-parra-chile-poet-dead.html', 'snippet': 'With everyday language, Mr. Parra and others defied high-flown poetic conventions with a directness that evoked the humor and absurdity of modern life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicanor Parra, a Chilean poet whose use of direct, colloquial and playful language, often for ironic and comic effect, pioneered the literary movement that became known as anti-poetry, died on Tuesday in Santiago, Chile. He was 103.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/25/obituaries/25parra1-print/24parra1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/25/obituaries/25parra1-print/24parra1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/25/obituaries/25parra1-print/24parra1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/25/obituaries/25parra1-print/24parra1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/25/obituaries/25parra1-print/24parra1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/25/obituaries/25parra1-print/24parra1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/25/obituaries/25parra1-print/24parra1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nicanor Parra, Chilean Voice in an ‘Anti-Poet’ Movement, Dies at 103', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nicanor Parra, Chilean Voice in an ‘Anti-Poetry’ Movement, Dies at 103', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parra, Nicanor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-23T23:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sewell Chan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sewell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a6b4e3d-ced3-5c38-95ee-fc3c493c03ef', 'word_count': 1282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a6b4e3d-ced3-5c38-95ee-fc3c493c03ef'}, {'abstract': 'Bite marks on fossils found on an atoll near eastern Africa suggest that this paradise for the world’s most common giant tortoise may have once been a much scarier place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/23/science/fossils-crocodiles-tortoises.html', 'snippet': 'Bite marks on fossils found on an atoll near eastern Africa suggest that this paradise for the world’s most common giant tortoise may have once been a much scarier place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today, Aldabra Atoll, an island in the Indian Ocean near Madagascar and Tanzania, is a predator-free paradise for more than 100,000 giant tortoises. Gone are the seafarers who over-hunted them to near extinction in the 18th and 19th centuries. Gone too are the large crocodiles that may have preyed upon them in prehistoric times, as a new study suggests.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/science/24TB-FOSSIL1/merlin_132772493_39b0dec3-a928-4c26-b94c-9f013eebbad7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/24/science/24TB-FOSSIL1/merlin_132772493_39b0dec3-a928-4c26-b94c-9f013eebbad7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/science/24TB-FOSSIL1/merlin_132772493_39b0dec3-a928-4c26-b94c-9f013eebbad7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/science/24TB-FOSSIL1/merlin_132772493_39b0dec3-a928-4c26-b94c-9f013eebbad7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/science/24TB-FOSSIL1/24TB-FOSSIL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/24/science/24TB-FOSSIL1/24TB-FOSSIL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/science/24TB-FOSSIL1/24TB-FOSSIL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ancient Crocodiles Once Feasted on Giant Tortoises on This Island', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trouble in Paradise: Description Released Of Giant Turtle’s Killer: 11 Feet Long, Big Teeth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aldabra Atoll (Seychelles)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turtles and Tortoises', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crocodiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fossils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Society Open Science (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indian Ocean', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seychelles Islands', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hansen, Dennis', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheyer, Torsten M', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-24T00:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas St. Fleur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'St', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b172453-2da3-594d-8eb2-9b78c85a0782', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b172453-2da3-594d-8eb2-9b78c85a0782'}, {'abstract': 'Climate change is adding to Iran’s disruptions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/23/opinion/trump-iran-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'Climate change is adding to Iran’s disruptions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After violent protests recently exploded across Iran, President Trump vowed to differentiate himself from President Barack Obama by openly tweeting his support for the demonstrators. It had no effect, though. One reason is that Trump could never send the really killer tweets — the ones that might h