52d'}, {'abstract': 'In a nation with a history of excluding indigenous people, the selection of D’Arcy Short selection for a set of Twenty20 internationals was a powerful symbol of change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/24/sports/cricket/australia-cricket-indigenous.html', 'snippet': 'In a nation with a history of excluding indigenous people, the selection of D’Arcy Short selection for a set of Twenty20 internationals was a powerful symbol of change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PERTH, Australia — For six months in 1868, a squad made up exclusively of Indigenous Australians went on a cricket tour of Britain, the first trip of its kind by an Australian team. The squad performed well, but the trip was never repeated. A year later, the Australian authorities gained complete control over the residence, employment and marriage of their country’s Indigenous people, the start of a heavy-handed form of oversight that rendered future tours impossible.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/sports/cricket/24cricket1/24cricket1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/24/sports/cricket/24cricket1/24cricket1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/sports/cricket/24cricket1/24cricket1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/sports/cricket/24cricket1/24cricket1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None,