g sea levels are forcing the country of Kiribati to make difficult choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five years ago, I could not locate the Republic of Kiribati on a map. Yet last month, I spent Christmas with its former president, Anote Tong, and his family in their beautiful ancestral homeland. In just a few years, the citizens of this low-lying Pacific atoll nation have profoundly affected my outlook on our planet and its prospects. The latest climate estimates project that sea levels could rise as much as six feet within this century, threatening to put Kiribati under water. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sinking Islands, Floating Nation', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kiribati', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-24T21:08:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthieu Rytz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthieu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rytz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc689afd-fd60-51eb-9182-014a8bb9c3f8', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc689afd-fd60-51eb-9182-014a8bb9c3f8'}, {'abstract': 'The British post-punk band’s main songwriter and vocalist has died at 60. Hear a dozen songs from one of the most daunting catalogs in rock.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/24/arts/music/mark-e-smith-the-fall-best-songs.html', 'snippet': 'The British post-punk band’s main songwriter and vocalist has died at 60. Hear a dozen songs from one of the most daunting catalogs in rock.', 'lead_paragraph':