': 'By Robert Ito', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ito', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cebe41b3-bdab-5ee1-bb4f-d68cc81e64ad', 'word_count': 1090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cebe41b3-bdab-5ee1-bb4f-d68cc81e64ad'}, {'abstract': 'Leelee Kimmel, who used to act under her maiden name, Sobieski, opens her first solo show, of paintings and a virtual reality film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/26/t-magazine/leelee-sobieski-kimmel-art.html', 'snippet': 'Leelee Kimmel, who used to act under her maiden name, Sobieski, opens her first solo show, of paintings and a virtual reality film.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I love crosshatching,” said the painter Leelee Kimmel, walking around her Upper East Side studio on a recent morning. The space is a converted prewar apartment, and her large, spattery abstract paintings provide a sharp contrast to the clean moldings. “We’re the generation of crosshatching, when you think about it,” she added. “Because we’re always hashtagging everything.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/t-magazine/art/24tmag-leelee-slide-CJJL/24tmag-leelee-slide-CJJL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/24/t-magazine/art/24tmag-leelee-slide-CJJL/24tmag-leelee-slide-CJJL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/24/t-magazine/art/24tmag-leelee-slide-CJJL/24tmag-leelee-slide-CJJL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'cap