erson': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Foley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b11ee7a1-e2b8-5cda-a5fc-89fd3380d37e', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b11ee7a1-e2b8-5cda-a5fc-89fd3380d37e'}, {'abstract': 'Wealthy Russians are on an aggressive lobbying push in fear that they will be penalized by a Washington intent on punishing Moscow’s aggressions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/26/us/politics/russia-oligarchs-list-sanctions.html', 'snippet': 'Wealthy Russians are on an aggressive lobbying push in fear that they will be penalized by a Washington intent on punishing Moscow’s aggressions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — It was all but ignored last year when it was wrapped into a sanctions law punishing Russian aggressions. But in recent weeks, a requirement that the United States identify Russian oligarchs in a public list has set off a cavalcade of anxious lobbying across Washington by those who fear their links to the Kremlin will jeopardize their financial well-being.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/27/us/politics/27dc-oligarchs1/merlin_131892872_a9c18ae0-d6db-400e-981f-c99f43b688a7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/27/us/politics/27dc-oligarchs1/merlin_131892872_a9c18ae0-d6db-400e-981f-c99f43b688a7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/27/us/politics/27dc-oligarchs1/merlin_131892872_a9c18ae0-d6db-400e-981f-c99f43b688a7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', '