 outcry — while thrilling some of the president’s supporters who were pleased by his swift fulfillment of a campaign pledge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/27/opinion/27soerensWeb/merlin_117398474_5f8877f4-72bb-4295-a7d7-8804ef864322-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/27/opinion/27soerensWeb/merlin_117398474_5f8877f4-72bb-4295-a7d7-8804ef864322-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/27/opinion/27soerensWeb/merlin_117398474_5f8877f4-72bb-4295-a7d7-8804ef864322-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/27/opinion/27soerensWeb/merlin_117398474_5f8877f4-72bb-4295-a7d7-8804ef864322-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/27/opinion/27soerensWeb/27soerensWeb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/27/opinion/27soerensWeb/27soerensWeb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/27/opinion/27soerensWeb/27soerensWeb-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will America Stand Again With the World’s Refugees?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicke