 just call myself “human,” but that default is white.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/27/opinion/sunday/why-do-you-say-youre-black.html', 'snippet': 'I was asked to just call myself “human,” but that default is white.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I went away to college at Princeton, 70 miles from where I grew up in New Jersey, I studied foreign languages, which is where I felt the most confident. I made friends with other black women and people of color, and we served as mental and emotional support for one another. I also met a 40-something European woman who became a crucial part of my college experience.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/opinion/sunday/28jerkins/28jerkins-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/28/opinion/sunday/28jerkins/28jerkins-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/opinion/sunday/28jerkins/28jerkins-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/opinion/sunday/28jerkins/28jerkins-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1414, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/opinion/sunday/28jerkins/28jerkins-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/28/opinion/sunday/28jerkins/28jerkins-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank