', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellsberg, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pentagon Papers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Post (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-28T15:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a330d7dd-3987-5d2d-8e3f-f082d1fa51cc', 'word_count': 1339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a330d7dd-3987-5d2d-8e3f-f082d1fa51cc'}, {'abstract': 'A vegetable-forward risotto, a garlicky beef-stir fry, mushroom quesadillas: Many delicious meals await at NYT Cooking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/28/dining/what-to-cook-this-week-newsletter.html', 'snippet': 'A vegetable-forward risotto, a garlicky beef-stir fry, mushroom quesadillas: Many delicious meals await at NYT Cooking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. A week ago, I was asking you to make my new recipe for sausage risotto with parsley for Sunday dinner. And I hope you did because it’s great. This week, though, I hacked the recipe, adding a lot of baby kale to the rice just before I served the meal, and if possible that turned out to be even more delicious than the original, with swirls of soft green amid the creamy grains of rice. So maybe this evening you could make the dish again or for the first time in this new, vegetable-forward way, and enjoy a very fine meal? Omit the sausage if you like. It’s flexible excellence, a fantastical feed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/magazine/28mag-eat1-copy/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/28/magazine/28mag-eat1-copy/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/magazine/28mag-eat1-copy/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/magazine/28mag-eat1-copy/28mag-28eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/magazine/28mag-eat1-copy/28mag-eat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/01/28/magazine/28mag-eat1-copy/28mag-eat1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/28/magazine/28mag-eat1-copy/28mag-eat1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Cook This Week', 'kicker': 'What to Cook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject'