nal': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7240ebb7-d239-5be5-a3f8-cdcfe8e5cb27', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7240ebb7-d239-5be5-a3f8-cdcfe8e5cb27'}, {'abstract': 'In an episode dominated by images of eyes, many of the most significant exchanges relied on little or no speech at all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/29/arts/television/the-alienist-recap-a-fruitful-partnership.html', 'snippet': 'In an episode dominated by images of eyes, many of the most significant exchanges relied on little or no speech at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sex and violence notwithstanding — those old standbys — prestige television series have several options at their disposal for generating cheap dramatic heat. One, a favorite of misguided workplace dramas and period pieces about bold and angry men, is to ratchet up the interpersonal conflict as high and as fast as possible. “The Alienist,” fortunately, is not that kind of show. Chronicling the quasi-official formation of Dr. Laszlo Kreizler’s dream team as its members pledge to track down a serial killer, the series’s second episode, “A Fruitful Partnership,” is true to its title.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/31/watching/31alienist-recap/31alienist-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/01/31/watching/31alienist-recap/31alienist-recap-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/01/31/watching/31alienist-recap/31alienist-recap-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 