rence in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-01-31T18:12:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Goldman and Nicholas Fandos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fandos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4131ce5-2a8a-540c-867d-7c6c16788bc8', 'word_count': 1609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4131ce5-2a8a-540c-867d-7c6c16788bc8'}, {'abstract': 'A law limiting the president’s power to fire the head of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau is constitutional, a federal appeals court ruled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/01/31/business/cfpb-director-firing.html', 'snippet': 'A law limiting the president’s power to fire the head of the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau is constitutional, a federal appeals court ruled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau’s director can be fired by the president only for cause, a federal appeals court ruled on Wednesday, restoring security to a job that has become a political lightning rod.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/02/01/business/01cfpb1/merlin_132522950_a8e2515a-9ad4-44e1-8783-643f4852942b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/02/01/business/01cfpb1/merlin_132522950_a8e2515a-